      "html": "<ul><li>The Welsh regulator is CIW. CQC is England. Scotland, Northern Ireland and Ireland each have their own.</li><li>CIW works under RISCA and its regulations. Always use the latest published version.</li><li>Inspections look at themes: wellbeing, care and support, environment, and leadership and management. CIW does not use a numeric grade scale.</li><li>A home does an annual quality-of-care review and keeps its statement of purpose current.</li><li>Adult safeguarding in Wales falls under the Social Services and Well-being (Wales) Act 2014.</li><li>Wales has Welsh-language duties, called the Active Offer. You can record how you meet them.</li><li>You answer in WhatsApp. No new app. No login.</li><li>Quickler is not a care records system. It holds no resident care data.</li></ul>"
